#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119653 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "38fce106-2ba8-554c-ace3-a5731d15a635" :question/math-academy-id "e-4949" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](images/f9/f9fe9fa5e18e286ac7e026df2667c7a8ce259cd2c0416efe85d66d2546358dfd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](images/9e/9e7b8bc888dbf7a764c0d5b9533758277b59e78d476a3cfe7bbfb2fcac7e7363.svg)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119654 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "74693316-2e5a-5821-87a5-fdc5b8719c82" :question/math-academy-id "e-4950" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119655 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1538dde4-ab62-502e-8efe-7f37628ab861" :question/math-academy-id "e-4951" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1bcf37-bd86-518e-aede-5addbc97699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260269} {:answer/id #uuid "59b5fe8c-5178-580c-8f7a-66873832ec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260642} {:answer/id #uuid "88058d4a-9c93-58e8-8a93-6bee79401fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261061} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a0b17a-e727-58fc-a945-2805ffef7542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261877} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90ee60-4b7a-54cd-af1f-b95d8d140b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff90ee60-4b7a-54cd-af1f-b95d8d140b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262116} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f58d02-2871-5109-a5be-ccd4ac8940b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aec3d295-8d51-5dda-ba42-3f14845dd36d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129095" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,-1,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6-4|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-22|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b6a76b-abc9-5372-a7ee-45b40832c99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259938} {:answer/id #uuid "2f08165d-5a4c-57f5-8879-fd9080d17d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260299} {:answer/id #uuid "34a5a6b7-596c-5939-a597-01b584e0736b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260345} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd14353-9e02-5403-b132-32e7153397aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260530} {:answer/id #uuid "adc6892e-d471-56a6-a370-4372feb2fafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b6a76b-abc9-5372-a7ee-45b40832c99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259938} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6db4bc9-8bdd-55c6-88be-86bab3785cc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "960aa08b-12d7-5431-bffd-ca432327fbf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129098" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,3,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨6,-1,5⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-2⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,-1,5).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,-1,5⟩-⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,-4,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-8-12|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{3} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38452af2-3463-5e38-b50f-517dc777cb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516229} {:answer/id #uuid "5269850f-0a46-56fc-897c-8ca14b3bd2c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516283} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d86851-66fb-594c-bde9-ae083bc8675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516452} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d74405-0178-5fb3-b7ac-3794c3723eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516592} {:answer/id #uuid "f61645ce-a87d-59da-b373-17d56da8e2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38452af2-3463-5e38-b50f-517dc777cb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516229} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab8132e-9ff7-5697-a331-2b7476559e4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7dcf7da-2297-59af-930a-8b2c6aff00d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129099" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,3,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨6,-1,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,0,-3⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,-1,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,-1,4⟩-⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,-4,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨4,0,-3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+0-15|}{\\sqrt{16+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|25|}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{5} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0746c2b1-8397-5ca4-bcc4-2be9ad0a31a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516126} {:answer/id #uuid "15641019-eb48-5052-a403-60ab3dfb5dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516154} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab0e081-5b86-55e7-981c-cd34744c91c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516200} {:answer/id #uuid "c462e695-1e8c-53ef-a160-41238e99ef40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516528} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ba0ca6-2710-5bc6-975d-35ed2106bb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ba0ca6-2710-5bc6-975d-35ed2106bb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516568} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fc70b3f-42c6-5104-a98d-c3951c9ae2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f033659-c7d6-5be9-97da-6420561e0286" :question/math-academy-id "q-129101" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(7,-2,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨5,-1,6⟩)\\cdot ⟨-6,3,2⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(5,-1,6).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,6⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-6,3,2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+3+6|}{\\sqrt{36+9+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443241} {:answer/id #uuid "168db077-1d3d-5cb0-b6aa-9a45c778361c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443242} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2a87c7-4871-52b2-9751-1dcf545d8473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443246} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4b18bd-d214-5ab3-980a-bcf8c20a44a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443253} {:answer/id #uuid "a192f294-392f-523d-b854-34cf2ca91ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443241} :answer-field/id #uuid "161dc5e7-caef-534f-b118-60aceff59caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "072e9e45-d148-5a1a-9029-08725d744a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-129126" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,4,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩=9.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩ & =9 \\\\ -3x+y+z & =9 \\\\ z & =9+3x-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+3(1)-(1)=11.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(1,1,11)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,11⟩-⟨-3,4,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-3+4|}{\\sqrt{9+1+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-11|}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b8c44f-f4d9-57d8-90d2-99d7decf9188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443244} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1d2c94-d43d-5c24-a663-9d1fbcba711f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443252} {:answer/id #uuid "acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443256} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d5ba1e-9709-5d81-81a8-a2db338b2a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443257} {:answer/id #uuid "e134b035-3648-5a34-a02a-44af5b1b5f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443256} :answer-field/id #uuid "3647b522-cc39-5b80-86fd-13996ce4e48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee5f2c99-4524-5cc2-872a-3bdd6d04d82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129142" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,2,6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩=8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2x+4y+4z & =8 \\\\ 4z & =8+2x-4y \\\\ z & =2+\\frac{x}{2}-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2+\\frac{2}{2}-1=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,1,2)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,2⟩-⟨-3,2,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|5\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-4-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{6} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1b5af0-a05c-505e-b5bf-10afc44fa4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476267} {:answer/id #uuid "3016c831-e8f4-5651-b74c-6377c71dd95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476309} {:answer/id #uuid "4275d3b1-6448-558a-b4a5-a4d62b2ac4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476347} {:answer/id #uuid "cebc6772-d1ae-5b50-bd1a-7a34f67a24f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476663} {:answer/id #uuid "dc5a4b5d-4377-54c9-bfe2-c832ba673c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc5a4b5d-4377-54c9-bfe2-c832ba673c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476700} :answer-field/id #uuid "adece7a5-0744-52d2-a422-6e0bf364c79d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf386a8a-8501-5e3e-a330-283d65ae0e3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129154" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,3,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x-3y+6z=16.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-2$ and $y=0$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-3y+6z & =16 \\\\ -2(-2)-3(0)+6z & =16 \\\\ 6z & =12 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-2,0,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-2,0,2⟩-⟨5,3,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,-3,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-7)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+(-5)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(6)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|14+9-30|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c4eecf-296e-5516-b53c-79b78ea2b9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260727} {:answer/id #uuid "db5f3fd7-fa3c-5df3-959c-4c7dfb2a5bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261814} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d44888-330f-5d97-813d-d06228ec63cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261997} {:answer/id #uuid "f962b70f-c02d-55ba-a6e4-84a85c82d4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262053} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9efcc2-19b9-54f0-bfe5-a15e71fd1354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f962b70f-c02d-55ba-a6e4-84a85c82d4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262053} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b182d-b8bf-588a-b715-8c9ecc4e2585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "091a2bf6-b258-57c8-a9fa-cfb6d9f29751" :question/math-academy-id "q-129161" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,2,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x+2y-4z=18.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y-4z & =18 \\\\ 4(2)+2(1)-4z & =18 \\\\ -4z & =8 \\\\ z & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,1,-2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨-7,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,2,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|9\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36-2+20|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|54|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{6} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c91748b-039e-5eb9-a37e-a538a11b547b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259994} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9b3c3c-b4f8-526a-9901-0c30d02dc50b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260689} {:answer/id #uuid "ad8f1a7d-4a09-5032-a136-33ad7657156e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261398} {:answer/id #uuid "e02b39e4-a270-5bce-b071-29e9f45c2040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261855} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ac539e-67e6-579d-a5b0-ddb5f34a0f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e02b39e4-a270-5bce-b071-29e9f45c2040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261855} :answer-field/id #uuid "d63e23f4-baa1-51c3-b321-bbcaaaa933a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "358dc254-c65c-55e3-933d-25bd9221af6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129165" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,4,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+2y+z=6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y+z & =6 \\\\ -2(1)+2(1)+z & =6 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,6)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,6⟩-⟨-1,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,2,1⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2+11\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4-6+11|}{\\sqrt{4+4+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b72bdaf-c17d-5a6f-a26c-13328e45c2b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260407} {:answer/id #uuid "63966b3b-7d0f-548b-957a-4189afb5ebfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260734} {:answer/id #uuid "654695db-ae2f-5c0a-8492-ff72aa97f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260751} {:answer/id #uuid "ae41e977-6f41-536e-a881-63dadca54693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261412} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ec70a3-7571-53d4-a32a-f4786362a4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63966b3b-7d0f-548b-957a-4189afb5ebfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260734} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0d9b85-acc6-5956-920a-859f666ff369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fc468d7-8c5a-51cb-a422-a6e8deebdd30" :question/math-academy-id "q-129166" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,3,-6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-x+2y+2z=8.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+2y+2z & =8 \\\\ -1(-2)+2(1)+2z & =8 \\\\ 2z & =4 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-2,1,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-2,1,2⟩-⟨-2,3,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 2+8\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0-4+16|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1367d4c3-b5b1-5690-aab2-44985cf01bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305319} {:answer/id #uuid "24668b28-99b9-5e54-a0c4-bc028c4820c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305498} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9d610b-76c5-572b-a11e-883ee62d0ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305730} {:answer/id #uuid "74516533-ce85-5ad6-abd6-3d0bfcce4ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306254} {:answer/id #uuid "c88bd5db-6ebf-5c09-b65a-02699a419dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24668b28-99b9-5e54-a0c4-bc028c4820c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305498} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6643fe3-e25b-594a-a4db-390d58331c15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cc5509e-3cff-5470-9ead-3ffe928da922" :question/math-academy-id "q-33451" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2,0,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,3,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4+6+18|}{\\sqrt{1+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|28|}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bbe24cf-fd8c-5f01-815b-71665908e829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366353} {:answer/id #uuid "864ae216-298f-5e6d-99b0-5743a693bda7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366354} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a49331-9463-54aa-b366-f0c946484cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366355} {:answer/id #uuid "59380b81-7c36-5c7e-97a6-e6c52c1c309b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366356} {:answer/id #uuid "45119e6d-8467-53d2-8d4f-1dff9a2160d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bbe24cf-fd8c-5f01-815b-71665908e829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366353} :answer-field/id #uuid "030f319e-0c23-5f25-ab63-9b411cec6724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92e09859-2a3a-5255-8ffb-72547639c5f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80113" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,-4,-8)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,1⟩=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,1⟩ & =3 \\\\ -2x+4y+z & =3 \\\\ z & =3+2x-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=3+2(1)-4(1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(1,1,1)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-3,-4,-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,5,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-8+20+9|}{\\sqrt{4+16+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "529cadbf-44d1-50b2-8c20-a9e272e22eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346057} {:answer/id #uuid "5889a9dd-d93f-5d3e-9d82-5347ba316df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346111} {:answer/id #uuid "88fb52ad-2071-5801-963f-3a749de660f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346540} {:answer/id #uuid "967e30a0-e60c-522f-a7eb-07ded0736475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346667} {:answer/id #uuid "f5938001-9365-567e-a131-44fd2b8da5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889a9dd-d93f-5d3e-9d82-5347ba316df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346111} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d59c58c-d76d-581e-8244-df4e793dba6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d51e9464-bbda-5ef7-95c6-2040c203954f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80115" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27496ca3-7fad-5a26-b5da-f602f9ca180b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345703} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6421f7-33b1-5c65-8910-c35b1c7a0bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346173} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfaae5e-dea8-5bfb-9c02-5fac3d7fa85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{109}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346455} {:answer/id #uuid "91d47231-c5cc-56c3-bf8e-35af3b2e786f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346627} {:answer/id #uuid "aae3eb0c-955f-52e9-abf1-f02ce3d8e415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dfaae5e-dea8-5bfb-9c02-5fac3d7fa85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{109}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346455} :answer-field/id #uuid "022c53e2-a752-5b98-a9ef-cff9a3af128a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6801290-8008-514c-8914-c43c32373fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-80116" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-6,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩=24.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩ & =24 \\\\ -8x+6y+3z & =24 \\\\ 3z & =24+8x-6y \\\\ z & =8+\\frac{8}{3}x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=3$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=8+\\frac{8}{3}(3)-2(1)=14.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(3,1,14)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,1,14⟩-⟨8,-6,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,7,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-8,6,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot (-8)+7\\cdot 6+9\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+42+27|}{\\sqrt{64+36+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|109|}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10263ca4-b8bb-5a2d-9cb0-a6cb6798e4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345488} {:answer/id #uuid "3fee28ed-fd4e-5e57-aea2-936eead49d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345901} {:answer/id #uuid "41336bd9-815f-549b-befc-b646e89179a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345907} {:answer/id #uuid "b507ac70-f33c-5dda-9141-f543ced2a2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346928} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c2d75f-e4ec-55e7-b876-ff7f73776f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7c2d75f-e4ec-55e7-b876-ff7f73776f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347546} :answer-field/id #uuid "81c6cb45-6adc-5f19-b537-ff2e27ce7534" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0953b145-a938-579d-a5dc-6946f5364a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-80122" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,11,10)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x-4y+4z=16.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y+4z & =16 \\\\ -2(2)-4(3)+4z & =16 \\\\ 4z & =32 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,8⟩-⟨-1,11,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-8,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,-4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-2)+(-8)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+32-8|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,18\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
